From 32aebca51866af362de42bc3bb928151549eb566 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:07:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PointWiseModel: integration by batches on the device

A point-wise model generated by the generic-parallel interface for the
device enabled in MFEM (for instance with the cuda backend) was integrated
by MGIS on the host, which fails: the computations of such a model only
access the memory of the device. It is now integrated by batches on the
device, as the behaviours of the behaviour integrators, then the copies of
its arrays on the host are made valid for reading, the other models
reading its states on the host (for instance as external state variables
given with the EXTERNAL_STORAGE mode, as in the example ex8 of
mfem-mgis-examples). Its update and its revert remain made on the host.

The construction of the view of MGIS on the copies of the arrays of a
material on the device (states, material properties, external state
variables and mass density copied to the device), made by
BehaviourIntegratorBase::integrateBatchOnDevice, is moved to
Material::makeDeviceView, and the criterion of the integration on the
device to the free function isIntegratedByBatchesOnDevice, both being
used by BehaviourIntegratorBase and PointWiseModel.

MaterialArraysTest: the point-wise model is also integrated over two time
steps, with an update in between, with the library generated by the
generic-parallel interface for the device of the test (openmp on the host
and on the debug device, where the integration on the device is
exercised and the host copies are protected, cuda on the GPU): the copy on
the device of the results is valid (integration on the device), and their
copy on the host is read without synchronization. The model
UO2Shrinkage_RAPHAEL2008 is added to the generic-parallel libraries of
the tests (library GenericParallelUO2).
